,\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-11T08:46:00.498Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-11T09:20:05.003Z\"}\n---001---\n{\"command\":\"epic-fix\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"blocked\",\"outcome\":\"blocked\",\"errors\":[{\"code\":\"PROVIDER_STALLED\",\"message\":\"Provider execution stalled for claude-code.\",\"detail\":\"Provider stalled after 1916036ms without sufficient output activity.\"}],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/fix/001-fix-result.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-11T08:13:38.673Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-11T08:45:34.769Z\"}\n---BATCH001---\n# Epic 02 Fix Batch 001 — from canonical epic review 001 (both blockers)\n\nImpl-lead rulings are embedded per item; build to these decisions.\n\n- [ ] **EPIC-02-BLOCK-001 — Scope the scheduler poke/touch seams per SDK instance.** Replace the module-global poke/thread-touch slots in `shared/context.ts` (and their global installation in `sdk.ts`) with per-SDK-instance delivery: work-queue `enqueue` must register its onCommit poke against the seam belonging to the SDK instance whose operation is running (e.g. carry the poke target on the OperationContext created by that SDK, not in module globals). Manual-mode SDK instances deliver pokes to a no-op (rows accumulate; AC-1.7). Background-mode instances deliver to their own scheduler. RULING: per-instance scoping is the chosen fix shape — do not clear-globals-on-construction and do not refuse multi-SDK construction. Multiple SDKs in one process (any mode mix) must be isolated: a manual SDK never auto-drains regardless of construction order. Add a regression test constructing background-SDK-then-manual-SDK on different threads in one process and asserting the manual thread's queued rows stay queued until explicit drain.\n- [ ] **EPIC-02-BLOCK-002a — Deleted-read filter on pair lookup.** `findPairedBlock` in `domains/messages/internal/forms.ts` (and any other pairing read used by handlers or intake's late-result lookup) must exclude deleted messages (`deleted_at IS NULL`), per tech-design §Mechanics' deleted-read rule (composition inputs and derivation reads exclude deleted records). A tool_call whose paired result is deleted derives outcome `unknown`, never the dead result's outcome.\n- [ ] **EPIC-02-BLOCK-002b — Pair counterpart joins the delete/edit cascade.** RULING (cascade contract): the call/result pair is a source dependency (AC-2.8's pair-as-source model); deleting or editing one half is a source change for the counterpart's summary. Extend `messages/internal/cascade.ts`: when a deleted/edited message has a call-id-paired counterpart with a tool-activity summary form, clear that summary to `pending`, bump its source version, and requeue it in the same cascade transaction (dedupe applies). The rebuilt summary derives from the live record only (with 002a, outcome reverts to `unknown` when the result is gone). AC-6.2's 'nothing else changes' bounds the cascade across other turns/chunks; the paired counterpart inside the dependency graph is in scope. Add tests: delete a tool_result → paired call summary requeued, rebuilt outcome `unknown`; control: unrelated summaries untouched.\n- [ ] **Record the cascade-scope clarification** in the story 06 deviation table (or epic deviation notes): pair-counterpart summaries are part of the mutation cascade per impl-lead ruling epic-fix-001; cite AC-2.8 symmetry.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1b388d14-2b35-4b36-8c72-7c338ac5cd77","uuid":"4c1ab255-49b5-4557-b78d-c71dc2f92231","timestamp":"2026-06-11T09:41:25.051Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\"command\":\"epic-fix\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"blocked\",\"outcome\":\"blocked\",\"errors\":[{\"code\":\"PROVIDER_OUTPUT_INVALID\",\"message\":\"Provider output was invalid for claude-code.\",\"detail\":\"Provider stdout was not exact JSON.; raw stdout bytes=3132639; raw stdout preview=